## Fix 5 — caret preservation

React reconciles text but has no concept of selection, so restoring the caret is
unavoidably imperative. Keep it to one place.

Store the intended caret as a **logical character offset** into the element's
concatenated text — never as a node/offset pair, which does not survive a
re-render. Restore it in `useLayoutEffect` so it lands before paint and never
flickers.

```js
useLayoutEffect(() => {
  if (pendingCaret.current == null) return;
  if (document.activeElement === el.current) writeCaret(el.current, pendingCaret.current);
  pendingCaret.current = null;
});
```

Read the offset with a Range probe (`probe.selectNodeContents(el)`,
`probe.setEnd(range.startContainer, range.startOffset)`, then
`probe.toString().length`) and write it by walking text nodes with a
`TreeWalker`, subtracting each node's length until the offset falls inside one.
Handle the empty case: a styled run with no text has no text node, so fall back
to an element offset rather than throwing.

Also handle paste explicitly — `preventDefault`, read `text/plain` only, splice
it through the same pure reducer. Never let the browser insert clipboard HTML.

